Title: **LAST MUTANT STANDING**
Credit: An unofficial Marvel fan film
Source:
	If every Omega-level mutant in the MCU multiverse
	fought each other... what would happen?
Draft date: September 28, 2026
Contact:
	Est. runtime: 20 minutes
	Non-commercial fan fiction. Not affiliated with Marvel or Disney.

FADE IN:

INT. KAMALA'S BEDROOM - JERSEY CITY - NIGHT

Fairy lights. Avengers posters. A phone on a ring light, recording.

KAMALA KHAN (19), a gold BANGLE on her wrist, stands at a whiteboard covered in a tournament bracket: WHO WOULD WIN? MULTIVERSE EDITION.

KAMALA
(to camera)
Okay. Big one tonight. The multiverse is real, which means somewhere out there are people with no upper limit. So: if you put every single one of them in the same room --

Behind her, a glowing ORANGE DOORWAY traces itself into the air.

KAMALA
-- who would win?

The doorway swallows her mid-gesture. FWOOMP.

The phone keeps recording an empty room. Her marker rolls slowly across the floor.

SMASH CUT TO:

> **LAST MUTANT STANDING** <

EXT. SAKAAR - THE GRANDMASTER'S ARENA - DAY

A junk planet under a sky of churning wormholes. A colossal COLISEUM welded together from dead starships. FIFTY THOUSAND ALIENS howl in the stands.

The floor is one enormous RING of scorched steel. High above it hang the Grandmaster's gilded VIP BOX and a rickety COMMENTARY BOOTH.

The GRANDMASTER (ageless, gold robes, blue stripe on his chin) spreads his arms. Beside him, TOPAZ, his bodyguard, who has never once been excited.

GRANDMASTER
Hello! Hi! Welcome, everybody, every... tentacle! Tonight we find the grandest champion in the universe. Correction: in *all* the universes.

Topaz holds up a battered TVA TEMPAD, patched together with tape.

TOPAZ
Bought it off a guy.

GRANDMASTER
She bought it off a guy! It opens doors -- anywhere, any when. So I asked it for every mutant on the Omega level. You know what Omega means? Nobody knows where your power stops. No ceiling!
(points up)
I had the ceiling taken out. For them.

ORANGE DOORS open across the ring.

WATER surges out of the first one -- and JEAN GREY (30s) stumbles through, soaked, arms braced against a flood that isn't there anymore.

GRANDMASTER
From Earth-ten-thousand-and-something: Jean Grey! Telepathic, telekinetic, tele-everything!

A CHESS TABLE slides through the next door, two old men still seated at it: CHARLES XAVIER (70s, wheelchair) and ERIK LEHNSHERR -- MAGNETO (70s), in prison whites, not a speck of metal on him.

ERIK
Your move, Charles.

CHARLES
(eyeing the crowd)
I rather think it's someone else's.

GRANDMASTER
Magneto! And Professor X, who's technically not Omega, but --

TOPAZ
Machine rounded up.

Warm rain gusts from a door: STORM (30s), in gardening gloves, eyes flickering white. Then BOBBY DRAKE (20s), holding a smoothie that's freezing solid in his hand.

GRANDMASTER
Storm! She doesn't control the weather -- she *is* the weather. And Iceman!

BOBBY
I'm sorry, *I'm* Omega-level?

GRANDMASTER
Nobody told you? Professor, that's a failure of education.

CHARLES
We were getting to it.

A bald woman in black strolls out of the dust of another door: CASSANDRA NOVA (30s). Soft voice. Terrible eyes. She smiles at Charles.

CASSANDRA
Hello, brother.

CHARLES
I don't have a sister.

CASSANDRA
Of course you don't. You'd have had to look.

The next door ROARS like a falling mountain. Out of the rubble walks WANDA MAXIMOFF -- THE SCARLET WITCH (30s). The crown. The red eyes. A mountain's worth of dust on her shoulders.

The crowd goes dead quiet.

WANDA
I'm not a mutant.

GRANDMASTER
Machine says you are. It's a new machine.

Erik studies Wanda with an odd, uneasy familiarity.

ERIK
Have we met?

WANDA
No.

ERIK
Strange. I have the strongest feeling I ought to be disappointed in you.

WANDA
Get in line.

A chrome, atomic-age BASSINET floats through the last door and settles mid-ring. Inside: a BABY in a blue onesie with a white "4" on the chest. He blows a raspberry.

GRANDMASTER
Who ordered a baby?

TOPAZ
(reading the TemPad)
Franklin Richards. Earth-828. Omega.

GRANDMASTER
Send it back.

Topaz jabs the TemPad. It sparks. Nothing happens.

TOPAZ
Baby doesn't want to go.

GRANDMASTER
Fine! He's the mascot. Topaz, hold the baby.

TOPAZ
No.

GRANDMASTER
Topaz.

Topaz holds the baby. Stone-faced. He grabs her nose.

One more door spits out KAMALA, who faceplants in the dirt.

KAMALA
-- who would win?

She looks up. Seven Omega-level mutants and a baby look back.

TOPAZ
Kamala Khan. Earth-616. Machine says... clerical error.

KAMALA
I'm technically a mutant! My friend Bruno ran tests!

GRANDMASTER
Sure, but you're no Omega. Topaz, what's under Omega?

TOPAZ
Everything.

GRANDMASTER
You're a Beta. Beta-plus. You're on the roster -- rules are rules -- but you'd last two seconds down here. You look like a talker.

KAMALA
I have a channel.

GRANDMASTER
You're my commentator.

GUARDS haul her toward the booth. Others close in on the Omegas with glowing OBEDIENCE DISCS --

Erik lifts one finger. Every disc RIPS free, streaks through the air, and crushes itself into a ball of scrap at the Grandmaster's feet. CLANK.

ERIK
You brought me to a planet made of metal. Choose your next words carefully.

GRANDMASTER
Love the energy! But the door machine only opens for my hand. My warm, *attached* hand. So: rules! Leave the ring, or can't get up, you're out. Last mutant standing goes home -- anywhere, any when they like.

WANDA
Anywhere? A world where my sons are alive?

The Grandmaster glances at Topaz. Topaz shrugs, baby still attached to her nose.

GRANDMASTER
...Sure! Why not!

CHARLES
And the losers?

GRANDMASTER
Go back exactly where and when I found you. Unless the champion's feeling generous.
(beat)
They never are. Topaz, show them where I found them.

A JUMBOTRON shows the moment each Omega was taken. Charles and Erik at chess in a plastic cell. Storm, raining gently on her tomatoes. Bobby, mid-smoothie.

GRANDMASTER
Cozy. Lovely. ...Tuesday?

BOBBY
I was making smoothies.

ON SCREEN: Cassandra in a desert of ruins, a colossal machine charging a beam of blue fire straight at her.

CASSANDRA
(pleasantly)
Time Ripper. Eleven seconds.

ON SCREEN: Wanda, as a mountain comes down on top of her.

ON SCREEN: Jean, at night on the shore of a black lake, arms raised against a wall of water from a shattered dam. Behind her, a jet claws its way into the sky.

GRANDMASTER
Ooh. That's a lot of water.

BOBBY
(quiet)
That's Alkali Lake.

STORM
Jean. We were on that jet. We watched you --

JEAN
I know.

GRANDMASTER
So three of you die if you lose, and only one can win! Math!

CHARLES
Then we don't play. Jean -- the rest of us will step out. You'll win. You'll live.

JEAN
(eyes on Wanda, then Cassandra)
And them? One of us lives and two of us don't. That's not winning, Professor. That's choosing.

WANDA
(quiet)
Then I'll choose.

CASSANDRA
Oh, I *like* her.

She touches two fingers to her temple.

CHARLES
Everyone -- guard your minds --

Too late. Erik, no helmet, goes rigid, eyes milky white. So does Bobby.

CASSANDRA
Boys. Be darlings and clear the board.

INT. COMMENTARY BOOTH - CONTINUOUS

Kamala grabs an ancient microphone. In the VIP box next door, the Grandmaster lounges while Topaz rocks the bassinet with one boot.

KAMALA
(feedback squeal)
Hi, Sakaar! I'm Kamala! I don't know who anybody is!
(squinting down)
Wait -- is that *Wanda Maximoff?* From the Avengers? Why is she covered in *mountain?*

GRANDMASTER
She's had a year.

KAMALA
And why are Magnet Grandpa's eyes doing that?

GRANDMASTER
He's been hacked.

EXT. THE ARENA - RING - CONTINUOUS

Even possessed, Erik glares up at the booth.

Then he raises his arms. The ring BUCKLES. A thousand steel beams tear loose, swarm into the sky like knives -- and dive at Jean.

Jean throws up one hand. The swarm STOPS a foot above her head. A thousand tons of steel, trembling in midair.

KAMALA (ON P.A.)
Red just stopped a *building* with one hand!

Milky-eyed Bobby turns on Storm. Spears of ice erupt from the floor. Storm rises into the air, eyes blazing white, and a HURRICANE begins to turn above the arena.

KAMALA (ON P.A.)
On paper this is a mismatch. She's the weather. He's a freezer.

Bobby raises both hands to the sky.

The HURRICANE FREEZES. All of it. A mile-wide spiral of solid ice hanging over the arena like a frozen galaxy, lightning trapped inside it like veins in marble.

KAMALA (ON P.A.)
HE FROZE A HURRICANE! FROSTY IS OMEGA! FROSTY IS OMEGA!

Storm stares up at it. Then, calmly, she tears open the clouds -- and the SUN blazes through like a furnace.

STORM
Weather includes the sun, Bobby.

The frozen hurricane melts all at once. A waterfall the size of a city block crashes down on Bobby and sweeps him out of the ring.

CHIME. Bobby vanishes in orange light and reappears, dripping and clear-eyed, in a GLASS BOX hanging over the arena, labeled in six alien alphabets: LOSERS' LOUNGE.

BOBBY
Did I just freeze a hurricane?

KAMALA (ON P.A.)
YOU DID, FROSTY!

Mid-ring, Charles and Cassandra face each other, perfectly still. Two fingers to two temples.

INT. MINDSCAPE - CONTINUOUS

Endless white. CHARLES stands here on his own two feet. CASSANDRA plunges her hand into his forehead, up to the wrist. He gasps.

CASSANDRA
Let's see what's in here. Chess. Guilt. *So* much guilt. It's like a cathedral in here.

A hand seizes her wrist. JEAN.

JEAN
Get out of his head.

She drags Cassandra's hand free, then presses two fingers to Cassandra's forehead.

JEAN
See how you like it.

For one flash we see what Jean sees: a little bald girl, alone in a desert at the end of time, waiting for someone who never comes.

Jean hesitates. Then pushes. The mindscape SHATTERS like glass.

EXT. THE ARENA - RING - CONTINUOUS

Cassandra flies backward out of the ring. CHIME. She lands on her backside in the Lounge, next to Bobby.

BOBBY
Hey.

CASSANDRA
Don't.

Erik's eyes clear. Jean lowers the steel swarm gently to the floor, beam by beam.

Charles, gray with exhaustion, rolls himself across the boundary line. CHIME.

CHARLES
(from the Lounge)
I forfeit. I've no interest in your game.

Erik looks at his own hands. His face hardens.

ERIK
Never again.

Scrap metal shrieks in from every corner of the arena and assembles itself around his head: a HELMET. Crude. Jagged. Magnificent.

KAMALA (ON P.A.)
That is a *lot* of garbage-to-helmet experience.

Erik turns his back on the ring and looks up at the stands. Fifty thousand cheering faces.

ERIK
Look at you. Placing bets on whose kind survives.

He pushes up his sleeve. A faded number is tattooed on his forearm.

ERIK
I was given a number once. By men who also enjoyed watching.

The crowd falls silent.

ERIK
The show is over.

He raises his arms. The whole COLISEUM GROANS, every bolt on the planet straining to tear free --

A RED BLAST hits him square in the chest.

Wanda stands between Erik and the VIP box, red light dripping from her fingers.

WANDA
Break his toy and I lose my way home.

ERIK
Child, he's lying to you.

WANDA
Everyone lies to me. He's the only one offering anything.

Erik hurls half a grandstand at her. It turns to red mist before it reaches her.

ERIK
You can't get into my head.

WANDA
I don't need your head.

She closes her fist -- and for one terrible second, every scrap of metal around Erik stops recognizing him. He is just an old man, standing in a ring.

She flicks two fingers. He flies out of bounds. CHIME.

KAMALA (ON P.A.)
(pale)
I have been an Avengers fan my whole life. I have never been scared of one until right now.

Storm lands between Wanda and Jean.

STORM
Anger is the easiest weather to call. And the hardest to send away.

WANDA
I'm not angry.

STORM
No. You're drowning.

Storm calls down a dozen bolts of lightning. Wanda catches them bare-handed -- they turn RED -- and hurls them back, straight past Storm, toward the crowd.

Storm throws herself into their path and flings them skyward. A thousand aliens saved. The recoil throws her clean out of the ring. CHIME.

Smoke. Rain. Two women left standing: Jean and Wanda.

JEAN
I'm not going to fight you.

WANDA
Then step out of the ring.

A beat. Jean nods, turns, and walks to the boundary. She lifts her foot to cross it --

-- and it won't come down.

She strains. Her eyes flicker gold... then FIRE.

JEAN
No -- no, no -- let me *go* --

A second voice rises beneath hers. Vast. Ancient. Hungry.

JEAN
(not her voice)
We do not go back to the water.

A PILLAR OF FIRE erupts from Jean, punches through the clouds, and spreads into burning WINGS a mile across.

!THE PHOENIX.

In the Lounge, Charles presses his palms to the glass.

CHARLES
Jean, listen to my voice --

GRANDMASTER
(on his feet)
*Now* that's an Omega!

Wanda rises to meet it, crown blazing, chaos magic spiraling around her.

WANDA
You don't get to win. I need this more than you do.

THE PHOENIX
Nothing needs like I need.

They collide. Where red meets gold, REALITY SPLITS.

The sky over Sakaar cracks like a windshield -- and through the cracks, other worlds. A black lake. A falling mountain. A gleaming retro-futurist New York. A Jersey City bedroom where a phone is still recording.

KAMALA (ON P.A.)
That's... my room. That's my room in the sky.

EXT. BEYOND THE EDGE OF EVERYTHING

Past the last star, THE WATCHER, who has seen every ending there is, leans forward.

BACK TO SAKAAR:

TOPAZ
Sir. The sky's broken.

GRANDMASTER
It's a feature!

BOBBY
(in the Lounge)
Why aren't they stopping?

CHARLES
They can't. Omega means no ceiling. Neither of them will run out of power before the universe runs out of room.

In the booth, Kamala sets down the microphone.

GRANDMASTER
Why'd you stop talking? This is the good part!

KAMALA
I don't think anybody should be watching this.

A shockwave hits the stands. The VIP box SHEARS half off its moorings and tilts out over the ring.

GRANDMASTER
Topaz! Leave the baby, it's got a force field or something --

He yanks Topaz clear. The bassinet slides across the tilting floor, teeters --

-- and falls. Straight down. Into the heart of the fire.

Kamala vaults the railing.

Her bangle BLAZES. She sprints down the open air on violet hard-light steps, each one appearing a half-second before her foot lands. She dives -- a GIANT GLOWING HAND bursts from her fist and catches the bassinet a foot above the steel --

-- and she lands dead center. Between the Phoenix and the Scarlet Witch.

She throws a violet DOME over herself and the baby. Fire and chaos slam into it from both sides. It cracks instantly.

KAMALA
(to the baby, shaking)
Hi. I'm Kamala. I've got you. I've totally got you --

The cracks spiderweb.

KAMALA
(screaming up at them)
THERE'S A BABY!

Inside the fire, Jean's eyes -- her own eyes -- find them. A girl with no chance at all, shielding a child.

Wanda sees them too. A child, in the path of her power. Again.

WANDA
No. Not again.

JEAN
(her own voice again)
Wanda. *Up.*

Together they wrench their power off the dome and hurl it skyward: red and gold, twisting into a double helix a mile high --

-- straight into the broken sky. It SHATTERS wide open. Worlds grind against worlds. The planet shakes to its core.

Jean and Wanda drop to their knees, drained. The hole keeps widening.

In the flickering dome, the baby stares up at the broken, burning, beautiful sky --

-- and laughs.

His eyes glow. He reaches up with one tiny hand... and closes his fist.

The sky SEALS. Every crack zips shut, racing across the heavens. The other worlds vanish. Just ordinary, garbage-strewn Sakaar sky.

Silence. Fifty thousand aliens stare at a baby.

A single FEATHER of fire drifts down and lands in his open hand. It doesn't burn him. He giggles.

CHARLES
(in the Lounge)
...Oh my.

BOBBY
Did the baby just --

ERIK
Yes.

The Grandmaster dangles one-handed from the wreck of his VIP box, Topaz beside him.

GRANDMASTER
The baby was the -- the whole time?

TOPAZ
Yep.

The boundary line flares.

ANNOUNCER (V.O.)
Last. Mutant. Standing.

Everyone looks at the ring. Jean: on her knees. Wanda: on her knees. The baby: flat on his back.

And Kamala Khan -- singed, shaking, bassinet in her arms -- the only one on her feet.

KAMALA
...Wait.

GRANDMASTER
No, no, no -- that's not fair to the baby! He can't stand, he's four months old --

TOPAZ
She's on the roster.

KAMALA
I'm technically a mutant!

One alien starts chanting. Then ten. Then fifty thousand.

CROWD
KA-MA-LA! KA-MA-LA! KA-MA-LA!

In the Lounge, five Omega-level mutants turn to look at the Grandmaster. The glass CREAKS. In the ring, Jean and Wanda rise, and look at him too.

GRANDMASTER
...Champion! Love her. So sparkly.

EXT. THE ARENA - RING - LATER

The Omegas gather in the wreckage. The Grandmaster holds up the TemPad in his warm, attached hand.

GRANDMASTER
So. Champion. Where to?

KAMALA
Home. But you said the champion decides what happens to everybody else. If she's feeling generous.

GRANDMASTER
I did say that.

KAMALA
I'm feeling generous. Everybody goes wherever they want. Whenever they want.

Every head turns to Jean.

KAMALA
Jean. You don't have to go back to the lake. You could *live*.

JEAN
If I'm not at that lake, the jet goes down.
(to Storm and Bobby)
You're both standing here because I went back.

Storm's eyes are wet. Bobby looks at his shoes.

CHARLES
Jean --

JEAN
You taught me that, Professor.
(a small smile)
You just haven't yet.

KAMALA
But you'll --

JEAN
I don't stay down.

The feather in the baby's fist flares. Jean touches his cheek, then steps through her door.

EXT. ALKALI LAKE - NIGHT

The wall of water. Jean holds it back as the jet climbs to safety behind her. She closes her eyes. Smiles.

The water takes her.

Beneath the black surface, something ignites: fire, spreading under the lake in the shape of an enormous bird.

EXT. THE ARENA - RING - CONTINUOUS

BOBBY
Can I go back to Tuesday? I left the blender on.

He steps through his door, then leans back out.

BOBBY
(to Kamala)
"Frosty." I like it.

On her way through her door, Storm flicks two fingers at the Grandmaster. A little RAINCLOUD forms over his head and starts to drizzle.

GRANDMASTER
Hey.

Charles and Erik are already back at their chessboard.

KAMALA
Mr. Magneto, you could go anywhere. You don't have to go back to plastic jail.

ERIK
(studying the board)
Charles hasn't finished losing yet.

Charles glances at Cassandra, alone at the edge of the ring.

CHARLES
Kamala. Send her somewhere she isn't alone.

KAMALA
Where's that?

CHARLES
(ashamed)
I don't know. I never looked.

The chess table slides through its door, two old men already arguing about the position.

The baby gurgles and points. A door opens beside Cassandra -- not orange. GOLD. Whatever waits beyond it is warm and bright.

For the first time, Cassandra has nothing clever to say. She steps through.

Then there's only Wanda. The crown in her hands.

WANDA
(to the Grandmaster)
There's no world where they're alive. Is there.

Under his little cloud, the Grandmaster can't meet her eyes.

GRANDMASTER
The machine doesn't really do worlds. It does doors.

Wanda nods. As if she knew.

Then the baby reaches up toward her. Grabby little fingers. Wanda hesitates -- and lets him take one.

His eyes glow. So do hers.

EXT. SUBURBAN STREET - DUSK - VISION

A TEENAGE BOY with dark hair walks alone under the streetlights. Magic crackles at his fingertips -- a light Wanda would know anywhere. He's looking for someone.

EXT. THE ARENA - RING - CONTINUOUS

WANDA
(a whisper)
Billy.
(to the baby)
He's alive. He's in my world.

She puts on the crown.

WANDA
Send me back to the mountain.

KAMALA
The mountain that *fell on you?*

WANDA
I've been buried before.

She steps through.

EXT. MOUNT WUNDAGORE - CONTINUOUS

The mountain comes down in stone and snow and thunder. At the very last instant -- a FLASH of red light.

EXT. THE ARENA - RING - CONTINUOUS

KAMALA
(to the baby)
Your turn, little dude. You know the way?

He waves the burning feather like a rattle. She kisses his forehead. He dissolves into golden light, bassinet and all.

GRANDMASTER
So, before you go -- permanent commentator position? Dental. *Very* generous dental.

KAMALA
You kidnapped a baby.

GRANDMASTER
He came on his own!

KAMALA
Bye!

She steps through. The door snaps shut. The Grandmaster slumps onto the ruins of his throne, raincloud drizzling faithfully. Topaz sits down beside him.

GRANDMASTER
Ratings, though.

TOPAZ
Ratings were incredible.

GRANDMASTER
Book the baby for next season.

TOPAZ
No.

INT. KAMALA'S BEDROOM - JERSEY CITY - NIGHT

The door drops Kamala exactly where she stood: singed, dusty, hair wild. The marker finishes rolling and bumps the wall. One second has passed.

She looks at the whiteboard. WHO WOULD WIN? Then at the camera.

KAMALA
Update. If every Omega-level mutant fought each other? Nobody wins. That's what Omega means -- nobody knows where it stops. So the fight doesn't stop either. It just keeps going up until there's no sky left.
(beat)
The only way anybody wins is if somebody stops.

She looks down at her shaking hand.

KAMALA
Also, the strongest one was a baby. I can't prove any of this.

AMMI (O.S.)
Kamala! Dinner!

KAMALA
Coming, Ammi! Also? Iceman is *criminally* underrated.

She scrawls two words across the top of her bracket -- THE BABY -- and stops the recording.

> SMASH TO BLACK.

> **LAST MUTANT STANDING** <

===

> **MID-CREDITS SCENE** <

INT. BAXTER BUILDING - NURSERY - EARTH-828 - NIGHT

Chrome curves and atomic-age pastels. A mobile of tiny planets turns overhead.

SUE STORM (30s) leans over the crib. FRANKLIN sleeps, clutching a FEATHER OF FIRE. It doesn't burn him.

SUE
Reed.

REED RICHARDS (40s) appears in the doorway. Sees the feather. Sets his mug down very, very carefully.

SUE
Where has he been?

H.E.R.B.I.E., the family's hovering robot, beeps.

H.E.R.B.I.E.
Franklin has not left the crib.

Sue and Reed exchange a look. Franklin smiles in his sleep.

> CUT TO BLACK.

> FRANKLIN RICHARDS WILL RETURN <

> **POST-CREDITS SCENE** <

EXT. SAKAAR - THE GRANDMASTER'S ARENA - LATER

Wreckage. Topaz sweeps. The Grandmaster sulks under his raincloud.

A door bursts open. DEADPOOL strides out, chimichanga in hand.

DEADPOOL
OMEGA-LEVEL BATTLE ROYALE, BABY!
(takes in the empty arena)
Oh, come *on.* Who won? Jean? It's always Jean.

TOPAZ
It was the baby.

DEADPOOL
(beat; to camera)
Twenty minutes. They gave every Omega-level mutant in the multiverse *twenty minutes.* I got three movies and a Wolverine.

A second door opens behind him. WOLVERINE glowers through it.

WOLVERINE
I'm not Omega-level.

DEADPOOL
You're Omega-level *grumpy.*

SNIKT. The door closes on him.

The raincloud drifts off the Grandmaster, parks over Deadpool, and starts to pour.

> CUT TO BLACK.

> THE END <
